---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Cta from "../components/Cta.astro";
import { site, hours } from "../data/site";

const schema = {
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About Gill Gas and Electrical Ltd",
  url: `${site.url}/about`,
  mainEntity: { "@id": `${site.url}/#business` },
};
---

<Base
  title="About Gill Gas and Electrical Ltd | Bedford"
  description="Gill Gas and Electrical Ltd is a Bedford gas, heating and electrical company. Registered at 4 Aviation Way, Shortstown, MK42 0HU. Company number 14391379."
  path="/about"
  schema={schema}
>
  <main id="main">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> About</p>
        <h1>About us</h1>
        <p class="lede">A limited company in Shortstown, doing gas, heating, bathrooms and electrics across Bedford and Bedfordshire.</p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap grid-2">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Gill Gas and Electrical Ltd is the registered name. Customers and reviews often say Gill, or Mr Gill.
            Companies House lists the director as {site.director}, appointed on {site.directorAppointed}.
          </p>
          <p>
            The company was incorporated on {site.incorporated}. From that date until {site.previousNameUntil} the name on the register was {site.previousName}.
            An older Google review still uses the TSG name. It is the same business.
          </p>
          <p>
            The company’s own site says the engineer has more than 12 years in the trade, and that the work covers domestic and commercial plumbing, heating and electrics.
            That 12-year figure is the company’s, not a number we counted from invoices.
          </p>
          <p>
            Gas work is described as Gas Safe registered. Electrical work is described as NAPIT-approved.
            Ask to see both before a job starts. Check Gas Safe at <a href={site.gasSafeCheck}>gassaferegister.co.uk</a> and NAPIT at <a href={site.napit}>napit.org.uk</a>.
            We have not printed ID numbers on this site, because those numbers were not on the public pages we checked.
          </p>
          <p>
            For heat pumps, Gill Gas and Electrical Ltd, {site.postcode}, is on the Renewable Energy Consumer Code member list.
            You can look the name up on the <a href={site.recc}>RECC member pages</a>.
          </p>
          <h2>How a job runs</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>You call or send the details, including the postcode.</li>
            <li>We say if we can take the job, and give a free quote for planned work.</li>
            <li>You book a time inside the published hours.</li>
            <li>The work is done, and you get the paperwork that job needs. A boiler install, a landlord gas record and an electrical report are different papers.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            If you smell gas, do not wait for a callback. Leave the building and call the National Gas Emergency Service on {site.gasEmergency}.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <figure class="split-photo">
            <img src="/media/google/g03.webp" width="1200" height="1600" alt="Bank of domestic gas meters and pipework" />
          </figure>
          <h2 style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">Opening hours</h2>
          <p>Taken from the Google profile.</p>
          <table class="hours">
            <tbody>
              {hours.map((slot) => (
                <tr><th scope="row">{slot.day}</th><td>{slot.label}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <Cta title="Talk to us about the job" />
  </main>
</Base>
